<title>PORTUGAL: Production rises at Portugal VW -Ford plant.</title>
<headline>Production rises at Portugal VW -Ford plant.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Ford -Volkswagen AutoEuropa plant in central Portugal is raising production to 677 passenger vans per day in July from 612 in June and about 530 in January, a company official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Production is being increased because of improving demand in Europe,&quot; the official, who asked not to be identified, told Reuters.</p>
<p>The plant at Palmela, 50 km (30 miles) south of Lisbon, is Portugal's biggest vehicle manufacturer.</p>
<p>-- David Brough, Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
